**Verdict on the second review: all nine findings accepted, none disputed.** Three were reproduced by running a throwaway JVM test against the real kernel and layouts, six by reading the cited transitions.

- **F1 and F2 (reproduced).** Resuming one of two woken waiters leaves control set beside a remaining wait, or beside a queued completed wake. One instruction leaves the queue untouched and today's lift refuses it. My v1 rule R0 and the ready-queue refusal are withdrawn.
- **F5 (reproduced).** The stack-layout equation fails at every conditional's jump pc. The layout table has no entry there or at terminators, while the kernel holds the consequent's value.
- **F3, F4, F6, F7, F8, F9 (by reading).** Install children run unbounded inside the sweep. A tenure check after the slice discards the computed boundary. My grant-check instruction would have broken halted restoration. The refusal oracle, harness order, and document text were all wrong as I had written them.
