**Plan v2 in brief.** The task becomes a product: one activation, ordered waits, ordered completed wakes carried by a new `:ready` row, in two new task slots. Fuel propagates to every install child with a per-tree bound, and the guarantee is stated honestly as interruption between instructions with no wall-clock bound. On tenure loss the holder retains the newest pure state for inspection only. Recovery stays the last durable checkpoint and the documents state the loss. Stack layouts are defined at jump and terminator pcs with an ordered check and a dead-prefix rule for tail residuals. The harness lifts, lowers, relifts, then runs in an isolated world. The report carries the exact amended text for six design documents and a line-level inventory of every safepoint mention in docs, code and tests.

**Order and effort.** 6d-a first, then 6d-b and 6e in parallel. The estimate rose from 11 to 15 days. Eight owner decisions are listed with recommendations, and the defaults let 6d-a start as soon as module-pins commit 2 is on master. 6d-a is the slice to brief first.
